The key for interpreting these entries is in the same file:
WEAPON(name,app,kn,mg,bi,prob,wt,cost,sdam,ldam,hitbon,typ,sub,metal,color)

So the fly swatter is

named: "fly swatter", 
does not have a special appearance when unidentified (char *) 0, 
starts off pre-known (kn 1), 
is not magic (mg 0)
is not two handed (bi 0)
has a relative frequency of 2 (prob 2)
weighs 10 (wt 10)
base cost 3 (cost 3)
deals 1d10 damage to Small creatures (sdam 10)
deals 1d2 damage to Large creatures (ldam 2)
adds +2 to hit (hitbon 2)
deals bludgeoning damage (type B)
uses the paddle weapon skill (sub P_PADDLE)
is made of plastic (metal PLASTIC)
is green in color (color CLR_GREEN))

Creatures rate it above rubber hoses and bellow pick-axes in terms of how much they want to use one in combat (weapon.c).

Other than that, it is not mentioned elsewhere in slash'em's code, so it appears to be as the description says: Good to-hit and small damage, but low large damage.

It does not appear to do double damage vs insects

